speechtext:
I would like to ask the minister this question. I understand the government is proposing to reduce the tariff protection under tariff item 559g from 20 per cent to 17J per cent. Could the minister give us a little explanation on this?
28902-5-144}
Customs Tariff

Snow plowing equipment is not designed specifically for agricultural purposes but in many cases is used for such. I can remember many a hard winter when a lot of ranchers and farmers plowed the snow so that their cattle could follow up behind and eat the grass which remained. In those days a snow plow was a very vital machine to have around when a rancher was caught short of feed. The last few years have been pretty warm, I do not know whether or not because of the political activity in Canada, but they have not been so prominent on farms and ranches as in the past. But in the future no doubt they will be used to quite an extent by many farmers. I should like to know whether or not they would be included under machines and tools for use on tractors, including blades, loaders, rippers, and so on. Snow blowers are not specifically designed for agricultural use, but they are used for such in many cases, and they are made readily to attach to tractors. I wonder whether they would come under this head or not. Would they come in under that catch-all phrase or under the other catch-all phrase, which is:
All other agricultural implements or agricultural machinery, n.o.p.;
I have taken a great deal of time and I see it is nearly six o'clock, but I hope the minister and his officials will take this snow blowing equipment along with the other items I have mentioned this afternoon and give it some thought as to whether it is already included under "all other agricultural implements".
